\par \tab 
When this spell is cast, the wizard is able to understand the spoken words of a creature or read an otherwise incomprehensible written message (such as writing in another language). In either case, the wizard must touch the creature or the writing. Note t
h
at the ability to read does not necessarily impart understanding of the material, nor does the spell enable the caster to speak or write an unknown language. Written material can be read at the rate of one page or equivalent per round. Magical writing can
not be read, other than to know it is magical, but the spell is often useful when deciphering treasure maps. This spell can be foiled by certain warding magic (the 3rd-level }{\i\fs24 secret page}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 illusionary script}{\fs24 
 spells), and it does not reveal messages concealed in otherwise normal text.
\par \tab The material components of this spell are a pinch of soot and a few grains of salt.
\par \tab The reverse of this spell, }{\i\fs24 confuse languages}{\fs24 , cancels a }{\i\fs24 comprehend languages}{\fs24  spell or renders a writing or a creature's speech incomprehensible, for the same duration as above.
