\par Area of Effect: 30-ft. cube/level\tab Saving Throw: Special
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab 
This spell combines several elements to create a powerful protection from scrying and direct observation. When the spell is cast, the wizard dictates what will and will not be observed in the area of effect. The illusion created must be stated in general 
t
erms. Thus, the caster could specify the illusion of him and another playing chess for the duration of the spell, but he could not have the illusionary chess players take a break, make dinner, and then resume their game. He could have a crossroads appear 
q
uiet and empty even while an army is actually passing through the area. He could specify that no one be seen (including passing strangers), that his troops be undetected, or even that every fifth man or unit should be visible. Once the conditions are set,
 they cannot be changed.
\par \tab Attempts to scry the area automatically detect the image stated by the caster with no saving throw allowed. Sight and sound are appropriate to the illusion created. A band of men standing in a meadow could be concealed as an empty 
meadow with birds chirping, etc. Direct observation may allow a saving throw (as per a normal illusion), if there is cause to disbelieve what is seen. Certainly onlookers in the area would become suspicious if the column of a marching army disappeared at 
one point to reappear at another! Even entering the area does not cancel the illusion or necessarily allow a saving throw, assuming the hidden beings take care to stay out of the way of those affected by the illusion.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs28\cf6 Serten's Spell Immunity }{\b\fs24\cf6 
\par (Abjuration)}{\fs24\cf6 
\par }{\fs24 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx3600\adjustright {\fs24 Range: Touch\tab Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn/level\tab Casting Time: 1 round/recipient
\par Area of Effect: Creature(s) touched\tab Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab By use of this spell, the wizard is able to confer virtual immunity to certain spells and magical attack forms upon those he touches. For every four levels of experience of the wizard, one creature can be protected by the }{\i\fs24 
Serten's spell immunity}{\fs24  spell; however, if more than one is protected, the duration of the protection is divided among the protected creatures.
\par \tab 
For example, a 16th-level wizard can cast the spell upon one creature and it will last 16 turns, or place it upon two creatures for eight turns, or four creatures for four turns.) The protection gives a bonus to saving throws, according to spell type and 
level, as shown in the following table.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s5\keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx180\tx1800\tx3600\outlinelevel4\adjustright \b\cf6 {\tab Spell Level\tab Wizard Spell\tab Priest Spell
